11.4.5 Closed-Loop Control Algorithm Specification

The swarm implements a spatially distributed proportional-integral-derivative (PID) controller with non-negative dose constraints:

Control Law:[u(t) = K_p \cdot e(t) + K_i \int_0^t e(\tau) d\tau + K_d \frac{de(t)}{dt}] [d(t) = \max(0, \min(u(t), D_{\text{max}}))] [e(t) = C_{\text{target}} - C_{\text{measured}}(t)]

Where (C_{\text{target}}) is the clinician-set target concentration, (C_{\text{measured}}(t)) is the swarm-quorum consensus measurement, (d(t)) is the ligand release rate, and (D_{\text{max}}) is the hard safety dose cap. Integral windup is prevented via conditional integration clamping.

Spatial Distribution: Release doses are distributed across particles in inverse proportion to distance from the highest-concentration-error locus, creating a smooth spatial gradient rather than a point release, mimicking natural volumetric neurotransmission.

Sampling and Actuation Cadence (8 Hz sensing / 0.2 Hz actuation):





Sensing and quorum decoding: 8 Hz continuous (125 ms frames; four-phase interleaved particle readout at 2 Hz per particle, per §11.4.2 Stage 3)



Tomographic reconstruction: 8 Hz, frame-aligned to acquisition (design latency ≤ 85 ms, SLA ≤ 125 ms at P99)



Control computation: 0.2 Hz (every 5 seconds), deliberately decoupled from the 8 Hz sensing rate to avoid pharmacokinetic over-reaction. The higher sensing rate does not destabilise the loop because the derivative term (de/dt) is estimated by locally weighted regression over an 8 Hz-windowed history rather than from a single 125 ms frame; the channel is low-pass filtered at the control bandwidth so that frame-level noise cannot excite the gain margin



Release events: capped at 12 per hour per ligand type



Mandatory 15-minute clinician review pause after first deployment



Audit cadence: every 8 Hz frame is sealed by a SHA3-256 Merkle-DAG leaf through hierarchical commitment, so audit cost scales with the number of clinician-selected regions of interest rather than with the 64,000-voxel reconstruction grid

