11.5.2 Daubert Compliance Matrix

For each genomic or neurobiological claim introduced as evidence, the pipeline generates a structured report addressing all five Daubert factors:





Testability: Whether the theory or technique has been tested — cites replication studies, GWAS sample sizes, and independent validation cohorts.



Peer Review: Whether the theory or technique has been subjected to peer review and publication — provides PubMed IDs, impact factors, and citation counts for every analytical method.



Error Rate: Known or potential error rate — reports confidence intervals, positive/negative predictive values, and false-discovery-rate corrected p-values.



Standards Maintenance: Whether standards control the technique's operation — documents CLIA/CAP accreditation, software version pins (Git commit hashes), and parameter configurations.



General Acceptance: Whether the theory or technique enjoys general acceptance in the relevant scientific community — cites consensus statements, clinical practice guidelines, and meta-analyses.

